---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHead from '../components/PageHead.astro';
---
<Base title="CV · Josh Paper" description="CV: technical delivery and project management, AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner.">
  <PageHead kicker={['Curriculum vitae', 'London, United Kingdom', 'British citizen']} title="CV" />
  <div class="cv">
    <section class="row">
      <h2>Summary</h2>
      <div>
<p>
    Technical delivery and project management professional with three years at The Access Group, the largest
    UK-headquartered software provider. Run around 25 concurrent projects drawn from a 70+ client portfolio on
    retainer, including Bandai Namco, F1 Arcade, Wingstop, Five Guys and Itsu, owning delivery end to end from
    discovery and scoping through integration build to post-launch adoption against contracted hours and SLA
    commitments. Scoped a loyalty integration now live across 16 brands and 56 venues and built an AI-assisted
    intake system that cut project scoping from five working days to a few hours. AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner.
  </p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="row">
      <h2>Experience</h2>
      <div>
<h3>Acteol, an Access Company</h3>
  <p class="meta">Hospitality CRM platform within The Access Group.</p>

  <h4>Junior Project Delivery Manager <span class="meta">April 2025 to present</span></h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Own delivery end to end on around 25 concurrent projects, from single integrations to module builds, drawn from a 70+ client portfolio. Deliver against contracted hours and SLA commitments, managing client and internal escalations.</li>
    <li><strong>DRG loyalty integration (Pepper):</strong> Scoped the CRM-to-Pepper integration for DRG across 16 brands and 56 venues, defining how transactions flow into the loyalty engine and how points accrue, tier and redeem. Owned field mapping and pre-go-live validation with Product and Engineering; live and operating across all 56 venues.</li>
    <li><strong>Asana rollout, 60 users:</strong> Co-led company-wide implementation, designing AI task automation, workflow rules, and client request forms. Overdue task rate fell from 25% to 11%; scoping cut from five working days to three.</li>
    <li><strong>AI-assisted project intake:</strong> Built a client-facing intake form that benchmarks incoming briefs against several hundred historical projects, deriving what a complete brief looks like by category and flagging gaps back to the client until the submission is usable. Accepted briefs auto-create an Asana task via integration. Scoping cut further, from three working days to a few hours. After launch, demoed to 150+ stakeholders.</li>
    <li>Act as primary technical consultant for key CRM modules (Dashboards, Sales Portal and Feedback &amp; Enquiries), running kick-off, discovery and feasibility sessions, translating requirements into build specifications and sequencing delivery against Engineering sprint cycles.</li>
    <li>Draft Statements of Work covering scope, timelines, risk and resourcing, supported by UI mock-ups and workflow designs that align stakeholders pre-contract, then manage change control against contracted scope post-signature.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Project Delivery Executive <span class="meta">April 2024 to April 2025</span></h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Client feedback portal:</strong> Re-architected the portal to auto-close resolved tickets and redirect to FAQs, deflecting 40% of inbound volume and removing 5 to 6 days of manual triage per month from the support team.</li>
    <li><strong>Automated user creation:</strong> Replaced a manual HR and client-onboarding process with an automated provisioning system, cutting half a day of admin per week and shortening client go-live setup.</li>
    <li>Designed and delivered structured onboarding and training programmes, taking clients from launch through to platform maturity.</li>
    <li>Presented at quarterly business reviews, turning performance trends into recommendations that shaped client roadmaps and internal feature prioritisation.</li>
  </ul>

  <h4>Associate Consultant <span class="meta">October 2023 to April 2024</span></h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Owned a portfolio of CRM clients, running consultative account assessments informed by competitor and consumer behaviour analysis.</li>
    <li>Sustained a review cadence that surfaced needs early, reduced support dependency, and opened up-sell conversations.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Royal Academy of Dance</h3>
  <p class="meta">International dance education charity and awarding organisation, 13,000+ members worldwide.</p>
  <h4>Finance Assistant <span class="meta">July 2022 to October 2023</span></h4>
  <ul>
    <li>Streamlined multi-currency reconciliation. Redesigned how transactions were categorised, allocating transactions to the correct accounts on first pass, cutting the monthly reconciliation cycle from five days to two.</li>
    <li>Processed transactions and reconciliations across 3 currencies and 80 countries, working between the finance system and the operational data feeding it.</li>
  </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="row">
      <h2>Certifications</h2>
      <div>
<ul>
    <li>AWS Certified Cloud Practitioner · July 2026</li>
    <li>AWS Solutions Architect Associate · in progress</li>
  </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="row">
      <h2>Projects</h2>
      <div>
<ul>
    <li><a href="/builds/second-look/">Second Look</a>: iOS app for pausing impulse purchases (AWS). Capacitor and Swift front end; Cognito, API Gateway, Lambda and DynamoDB back end with server-side per-user data isolation.</li>
    <li>Howzit: serverless web app for contact management (AWS). Cognito, API Gateway, Lambda and DynamoDB with server-side per-user data isolation and least-privilege IAM.</li>
  </ul>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section class="row">
      <h2>Skills</h2>
